{"name":"Immortality","hex":"#945b7f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"immortality","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The condition of being immortal. \nNever dying","Never dying"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/immortality"}],"entries":[{"title":"Immortality","blocks":[{"text":"Immortality is the concept of eternal life and permanent resistance to death from natural causes. Some species possess \"biological immortality\" due to an apparent lack of the Hayflick limit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Fountain_of_Eternal_Life_crop.jpg/330px-Fountain_of_Eternal_Life_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immortality","wikidata":"Q193942"},{"title":"Immortality (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Immortality is a 2022 interactive film video game developed by Sam Barlow and published by Half Mermaid Productions. It was released for Windows and Xbox Series X/S in August, while Android and iOS versions were released via Netflix in November 2022. A macOS version was released in April 2023. A port for PlayStation 5 was released in January 2024."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d4/Immortality_%28video_game%29_cover_art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immortality_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q107225273"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Telomere_caps.gif/500px-Telomere_caps.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Telomere_caps.gif/500px-Telomere_caps.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Human chromosomes (grey) capped by telomeres (white)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATelomere_caps.gif"},{"srcset":"https://